WeftForge CLI — offline editable garment tools

mcp                                    local MCP stdio file authoring
new PROJECT
sample PROJECT                         original two-panel shirt (implementation fixture)
inspect PROJECT
inspect-sewing PROJECT                  authored groups, portions and rest stitches (JSON)
execute INPUT OUTPUT COMMANDS.json      one atomic shared command array
rectangle INPUT OUTPUT NAME X Y WIDTH HEIGHT
resize INPUT OUTPUT PIECE_ID WIDTH HEIGHT
curve-controls INPUT OUTPUT CURVE_ID X1 Y1 X2 Y2   absolute cubic controls in m
curve-controls INPUT OUTPUT CURVE_ID straight
split INPUT OUTPUT CURVE_ID T          interior curve parameter; preserves sewing
join INPUT OUTPUT CURVE_ID             shape-preserving join with next boundary
grain INPUT OUTPUT PIECE_ID RADIANS    warp: 0=+U, positive toward +V
stiffness INPUT OUTPUT MATERIAL_ID WARP WEFT   physical N/m
export-obj PROJECT OUTPUT.obj
export-svg PROJECT OUTPUT.svg
export-dxf PROJECT OUTPUT.dxf          exterior pattern boundaries in mm
simulate PROJECT OUTPUT.obj STEPS      f64 CPU XPBD, contacts always enabled
benchmark PROJECT STEPS                JSON measurements for the same solver
fit-benchmark PROJECT                  explicit 1 s zero-gravity assembly, 2 s drape
fit PROJECT OUTPUT.obj                same protocol, exports only after quality checks pass
recover PROJECT OUTPUT                explicitly load last valid recovery

Units: metres, kilograms, seconds; Y-up. Legacy seam fractions use curve t; sewing groups use authored arc length. All edits use the desktop command engine.
Simulation is currently a rebuildable state; projects store editable construction.
